  "title": "LS2b fix round 1: sanitize every free-text field rendered into the auto-handover section, not only titles",
  "spec": "Fix round of T-1612, answering security review T-1613 (request_changes, high). T-1612 added a one-line sanitizer (_title) for titles only. Other task-supplied text is still interpolated raw in orchestrator/handover.py: t['reason'] (failed group, ~line 134), hold_reason (~127), executor (~122), resume_hint keys, and e['task'], e['kind'] and the json data in the events tail (~249). A value containing '\\n## Foo' or '\\n<!-- end auto-handover -->' puts a heading or a fake end marker inside the section and brings the growth bug back.\n\nFix: route every interpolated free-text value in _render_section and its helpers (_goal_lines, _task_ref, the events tail, any other) through one sanitizer that collapses whitespace runs including newlines to one space and caps length (titles 160 chars as now; other fields keep their existing caps or 160 when none). Then, as a last guard in _render_section, assert or enforce that no rendered line other than the heading starts with '## ' and that the marker appears exactly once, as the last line.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_handover.py::test_render_sanitizes_reason_hold_reason_and_events passes: tasks whose reason, hold_reason and executor, and an event whose kind contains '\\n## Foo\\n<!-- end auto-handover -->', render with no line other than the heading starting with '## ' and exactly one end marker, the last line",
    "tests/test_handover.py::test_write_with_multiline_goal_title_does_not_grow passes",
    "tests/test_handover.py::test_write_keeps_sections_after_marker passes",
    "tests/test_handover.py::test_write_legacy_section_without_marker_runs_to_eof passes"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/handover.py",
    "tests/test_handover.py"
  ],
